{
  "requirement": "An application supporting tracked source inspection returns `Self::NodeData` for the requested path and selector. The SDK interns that data in the domain's cache to obtain `NodeId<Self>`. An unsupported or invalid address returns an error. The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item. For source identities the application can supply independently, implement `source_address` to recover the project-relative outline address from the domain identity. Other identities return `None`.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The marked tests cover each obligation of `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`.\n\n- **`source_node` returns `NodeData` for the requested path and selector.**\n  - In `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]`, a path and selector (`src/parser.rs`, `impl[Parser]/fn[parse]`) map through `source_node` and back through `source_address` to the identical `OutlineData`.\n  - In `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]`, the `TestDomain::source_node` hook records the items it receives. The test asserts that the visible selected file is mapped with an empty selector and that the mapped nodes (ids 7 to 10) appear as dependencies.\n- **The SDK interns the data to get a `NodeId`.**\n  - The `configured.rs` test compares dependencies against `domain.cache().intern_node(TestNode{id:N})`.\n  - `agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns]` asserts the dependency is `intern_node(\"source-node\")` for the data the domain returned.\n- **An unsupported or invalid address returns an error.** `direct_source_reads_preserve_mapping_errors_and_record_only_successful_returns` covers two cases: an unknown path and an unknown selector. Both return an \"unsupported source item\" error, with no dependency recorded and no read performed.\n- **The cache retains the address when the SDK maps a source item.**\n  - `TestDomain` in `configured.rs` has no `source_address` override, so it returns `None`.\n  - Even so, the test lets `read_node` use the listing entry, with `node` and `data` both present. That read returns the mapped snapshot (\"a source snapshot\"), not the disk contents.\n  - That works only if the cache kept the address from `list_sources`.\n  - `agent_node_addresses_round_trip_and_reject_inconsistent_identities_before_reads` adds node-id and path/location round trips.\n- **`source_address` recovers the address for identities the application can supply, and other identities return `None`.**\n  - The `sdk.rs` test asserts the `Some(method)` round trip.\n  - It also asserts `domain.source_address(&node) == None` for every other `HabeasNode` kind: requirement, reference set, selection, definition, citation review, site review, and a source node built from a generated resource that was never mapped.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap. `public_exports_match_the_appendix` is tangential and adds nothing needed.",
  "references": "1d29a32082b25d649b6110366e39b9fc87deb5e567f66edeb4008297385b5324",
